From 99bd3144c851a265a0de078ae0838e2fcf99e1a5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 06:04:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [Hades] Power menu: "Restart into Windows", for the next
 start only

On a PC with Windows and LibreELEC Hades, Windows comes first in the boot order of the UEFI firmware and Hades is
started for one start: from the boot menu of the firmware, or by "Restart into LibreELEC Hades" of the installer for
Windows, which sets BootNext. A plain restart then goes back to Windows; but where Hades comes first (installed inside
the PC and chosen first in the firmware), or where the firmware puts a USB drive first, it does not, and the way to
Windows was the boot menu of the firmware.

The new entry of the power menu of Estuary, under "Reboot", starts Windows at the next start, and only at that one: the
builtin RebootToWindows asks /usr/lib/libreelec/hades-bootnext to set BootNext to the entry of Windows that the firmware
already has (Windows Boot Manager, \EFI\Microsoft\Boot\bootmgfw.efi), which the firmware deletes when it uses it, and
then reboots as Reboot does. No boot entry is made, changed or deleted, and the boot order stays as it is. When the
helper does not answer that the firmware took the value back, the PC is not restarted and a notification says how to
reach Windows from the boot menu of the PC.

The entry is shown (System.CanRebootToWindows) where the system started by UEFI, the firmware has an active entry of
Windows in its boot order, and its variables can be written: what hades-bootnext.service leaves in /run/hades-bootnext
before Kodi starts. It is shown also where a plain restart starts Windows already (Hades started for one start): it is
then the same thing, said plainly, and the person who wants Windows does not have to know which way the firmware goes.
kodi.log says once why it is shown or not, which entry this start came from and what a plain restart starts, and what
the entry did when it is used.

RebootToWindows counts as a power-down command, so PVR can hold it back as it holds Reboot. The info number is 799, at
the end of the block of system booleans, away from the numbers that Kodi gives next. Strings: core 42240-42241,
translated in Estuary as 34240-34241 (es_ES, es_AR, es_MX).
